Really really minor spoilers about statues, figurines.


> 1. What do you do with statues and figurines ??
You apply figurines, and they become pets of what-ever type of
figurine they are.  I just learned something about statues.  If you
destroy one with your pickaxe, you sometimes get spell books among the
rubble.

> 2. Is it OK to eat a unicorn corpse?
It is fine to eat a unicorn corpse, although I always prefer to offer
them if I can.

> 3. Does anyone have any general strategies/philosophies for playing 
>    the game e.g. do you do the Gnomish mines ASAP, or go to down to 
>    dungeon level 10 and then do them; is it best to quaff every 
>    potion and read every scroll you get etc...
When you read scrolls and quaff potions is much a personal preference.
I personally like to have protective measures before I start quaffing,
(i.e. telepathy, poison resistance, from within a locked room)  and I
always find out if my scrolls are cursed before I read them, and I
drop all my flammable/explodable goods before I read them (in case of
fire)  The mines, however, are a must go.  You might occasionally go
down one or two regular levels in order to find an altar, but without
the goods that you will probably get from the mines (Blessed bag of
holding, pickaxe, luckstone, lockpick, stethescope, and on and on)
you will doubtfully last long in the dungeon.


